pseudo-Boolean proof version 2.0
* A version 2.0 order whose `aux` list is NOT empty, which is the one
* combination the corpus never had: the four version-2 instances with an order
* all write `aux` with nothing after it, and every order that does have
* auxiliary variables is written in version 3.0.
*
* The two features had never met, and they do not fit together. The version-3
* grammar reads the `aux`, `fresh_aux_1` and `fresh_aux_2` lists with
* `is_var_allowed = false`, so every name in them has to be an
* `AuxiliaryVariable` token -- `$`-prefixed. The version-2 grammar has no `$`
* at all: `legacy_v2::tokens::VariableToken` and `LiteralToken`, and the OPB
* and DIMACS formula parsers, all take names from
* `[a-zA-Z_][_a-zA-Z0-9\-^\[\]{}]+`. `-e` always emits version 3.0. So this
* proof used to verify at exit 0, elaborate at exit 0, and produce a version-3
* proof that does not parse:
*
*     Expected an auxiliary variable or `;` but found `q1` at line 7 col 7.
*
* The elaborator now renames each such variable to `$` + its name, in the
* variable-name table rather than at the point of writing, so that *every*
* occurrence moves together: there is one source of names, so there is no
* write site to miss. This instance is laid out to make that reach visible --
* `q1` appears in the `aux` list, in the `spec` constraint, in that `red`'s
* witness, and in the `def` constraint, and the transitivity block adds
* `fresh_aux_1` and `fresh_aux_2`, which the version-3 grammar constrains the
* same way. All of them come out `$`-prefixed, and the elaborated proof
* re-checks with the same verdict.
f 1
pre_order simple
    vars
        left u1
        right v1
        * the auxiliary variable, unspellable as `$q1` in this dialect
        aux q1
    end

    * a specification for `q1`, which puts the renamed name in a constraint
    * and in a witness as well as in the `aux` list above
    spec
        red 1 ~q1 >= 1 ; q1 -> 0 ; begin
        end
    end

    * `q1` in the definition too, so the rename has to reach `def`
    def
        1 ~u1 1 v1 1 q1 >= 1 ;
    end

    transitivity
        vars
            fresh_right w1
            fresh_aux_1 b1
            fresh_aux_2 c1
        end
        proof
            * 4: 1 ~u1 1 v1 1 q1 >= 1   (the definition, on u,v)
            * 5: 1 ~v1 1 w1 1 b1 >= 1   (the definition, on v,w)
            * 1,2,3: the specification, on q1, b1 and c1
            * 6: the negated goal, 1 u1 1 ~w1 1 ~c1 >= 3
            proofgoal #1
                p 4 1 + 5 + 2 + 6 +
            end -1
        end
    end
end

* reflexivity is auto-proven: the definition under `v1 -> u1` is
* `1 ~u1 1 u1 1 q1 >= 1`, a tautology.

load_order simple x1
p 1 1 +
load_order
output NONE
conclusion NONE
end pseudo-Boolean proof
